{"case_id":"T5035","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["configuration","API protocol","state","attack surface"],"confidence":99,"affected_functions":["spng_set_option","spng_get_option","require_bytes","write_data"],"reason":"H0 exercises PNG decoding through a non-encode-only context, but S1 adds an encoding-to-internal-buffer mode whose configuration, state transitions, destination validation, allocation growth, and error propagation are never reached. This is fuzz-worthy because SPNG_ENCODE_TO_BUFFER changes ctx->internal_buffer and ctx->state, while require_bytes() and write_data() handle attacker-influenced encoded sizes and memory operations under that mode.","evidence":["tests/spng_read_fuzzer.c creates ctx with spng_ctx_new(SPNG_CTX_IGNORE_ADLER32) and only calls read/decode APIs such as spng_set_png_buffer(), spng_decoded_image_size(), spng_decode_image(), and spng_decode_row().","H0 never calls spng_set_option() or spng_get_option() with SPNG_ENCODE_TO_BUFFER and never creates an encode-only context required by the check if(!ctx->encode_only) return SPNG_ECTXTYPE.","spng_set_option() adds value validation and state-dependent outcomes for SPNG_ENCODE_TO_BUFFER: negative values fail, non-encode contexts return SPNG_ECTXTYPE, state >= SPNG_STATE_OUTPUT returns SPNG_EOPSTATE, zero is a no-op, and nonzero sets internal_buffer and SPNG_STATE_OUTPUT.","require_bytes() adds if(!ctx->internal_buffer) return SPNG_ENODST and otherwise performs encoded-size overflow checks, buffer growth, realloc(), and write-pointer updates.","write_data() now propagates the specific require_bytes() result through encode_err(ctx, ret) before memcpy(ctx->write_ptr, data, bytes), behavior absent from H0's decoding path.","spng_get_option() adds observable reporting of ctx->internal_buffer through SPNG_ENCODE_TO_BUFFER, but H0 does not test the set/get protocol or resulting state."],"recommended_action":"Add an encode-focused fuzz target that creates encode-only contexts and fuzzes SPNG_ENCODE_TO_BUFFER set/get values and call ordering before and after output state, then drives encoding with varied image metadata, dimensions, formats, and pixel data. Exercise both configured internal-buffer output and missing-destination paths, checking SPNG_ECTXTYPE, SPNG_EOPSTATE, SPNG_ENODST, overflow/allocation failures, and successful buffer growth."}
